    "notes": [
      "Primary F4U-1D manufacturer/archive three-view visually inspected. Raster 1584 \u00d7 1016; measured original pixels are retained below.",
      "Plan is rotated 90 degrees relative to side: converted plan x = 492 - original image y; span offset = original image x - 313.",
      "The primary drawing labels 16 ft 6 in horizontal tail span and 12 ft 1 in landing-gear track; those values override measurement noise. Its 13 ft 4 in early propeller differs from later 13 ft 1 in Smithsonian example; the model uses the latter and records the variant difference.",
      "Wing front contour measured against shaft at original image y=795: root at y=810, minimum at y=834 near x=411, tip near y=797. Mesh z is the airfoil midline, not its lower surface.",
      "Fin and cockpit are separate from the tapered body. The late -1D clear sliding hood uses only end hoops and windshield framing; manufacturing sections, panel fasteners, and wheel extension kinematics remain approximate."
    ],
